# C8 control: the EARLIER relay TS geometry through OUR method and QM region.
#
# Seed: orca_stuff/cat/cat+H2O2+H2O/ts2/job.xyz -- the imported worker's relay TS
# (! QM/XTB r2SCAN-3c ALPB(Water) optTS freq, 9-atom QM1). That saddle is EARLY:
# C128...Oprox 1.946 A, C=O 1.259, with the PROXIMAL peroxide O bare and the H
# on the distal O. Ours (ts/optts_full, ts/optts_bridge) is later, C...O 1.73 /
# 1.61, with the transferring H on the proximal O. The suspicion is that the QM
# region did it -- theirs 9 atoms, ours 21.
#
# So: same seed geometry, OUR method and region.
#   ! QM/XTB B97-3c ddCOSMO(Water) OptTS Freq TightOpt TightSCF
#   QM1 = 21 atoms, neutral (H2O2), full system, no ActiveAtoms, no scan.
#
# Atom ordering note: the two 137-atom systems agree at every index except
# {131,134,135,136}, where theirs is H,H,O,O and ours O,O,H,H. The SET
# {55 58 61 64 120..136} is the same structural region either way, so the region
# transfers without remapping.
! QM/XTB B97-3c ddCOSMO(Water) OptTS Freq TightOpt TightSCF

%QMMM
QMATOMS
	{55 58 61 64 120 121 122 123 124 125 126 127 128 129 130 131 132 133 134 135 136}
END
Charge_total 0
Mult_total 1
AutoFF_QM2_Method GFNFF
END

%geom
  MaxIter 400
  Calc_Hess true
end

%output jsonpropfile true end

%maxcore 4000

%pal
   nprocs 8
end

* xyzfile 0 1 job.xyz
